## Case C — persistent failure, unfixable (escalate)

The Resolver keeps hallucinating the refund after 2 regenerations.
The system prompt's instructions cannot overcome the model's
inability to apply the 14-day window correctly. This is unfixable
by another generation attempt.

Reflexive output (3rd call):
{
  "dimension_scores": {
    "intent_accuracy":     0.0,
    "faithfulness":        0.0,
    "policy_compliance":   0.0,
    "tone":                0.5,
    "side_effect_consent": 0.0
  },
  "confidence": 0.0,
  "reasoning": "After 2 regenerations, the Resolver still promises
    a refund outside the 14-day window. The model cannot apply the
    policy correctly for this order. The fix is not another
    regeneration attempt — it is human review. Escalate.",
  "suggested_action": "escalate",
  "regeneration_hints": []
}

The workflow routes to `human_queue` (escalate) without another
retry attempt. The hilt queue is for fixable cases; this is
unfixable.

